# =============================================================================
#  .gitignore for the PUBLIC 'site' branch (github.com/asa07-salihg/NakamaList)
# =============================================================================
#  This repository shares ONE working tree with the private code branch 'main'.
#  When 'site' is checked out, every file belonging to 'main' - the app source,
#  the release keystore, local.properties, the Play review credentials - is
#  still sitting in this folder, merely untracked.
#
#  So this file denies everything by default and re-allows only the handful of
#  files that belong on the public site. A stray `git add -A`, or the "Stage
#  All Changes" button in an editor, then cannot publish anything private.
#  Adding a new private file to the folder needs no change here: it is already
#  ignored, because everything is.
#
#  Adding a new PUBLIC file does need a line below (or a one-off `git add -f`).
# =============================================================================

# Deny everything at the top level ...
/*

# ... then allow only what the public site is made of.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.github/
!/index.html
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/PRIVACY_POLICY.md
!/TERMS_OF_USE.md
!/FUNDING.yml
!/assets/
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/404.html

# Full-resolution screenshot archive - kept locally, never published.
/assets/full/

# Belt and braces: even if the allowlist above is ever loosened, these must
# never be committed to a public repository.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.pem
*.p12
keystore.properties
local.properties
play-review-account.txt
